# p532: independent probe of the pinned augustss/verse-semantics oracle
# (d0eababfb7a5662f40bc7de45a596cb925445b8d, the flake.lock pin).
# Purpose: re-derive issue #1 comment 2's claims from primary sources.
# Expectations below are derived BY HAND from the printed rules first
# (docs/VERSE-RULES.md sec. 3.4 = Figs. 13; Fig. 10 line 459 read from
# SPJ_Verse-figures.pdf, verified 2026-11-27), then the oracle is consulted.
# Each claim is pinned as an explicit value (house corpus convention); the
# `{wrong}` form pins "gets stuck" (tester/Main.hs:591).

# 1. Order is observable through all{} (Fig. 13 IterChoice nests in order;
#    SCHOICE line 1073: source | = ordered choice).  The two pins below make
#    all{2|1} != all{1|2} explicit; the third makes non-idempotence explicit.
testeq("p532-all-12",   pass) { all{1|2} }   { array{1,2} }
testeq("p532-all-21",   pass) { all{2|1} }   { array{2,1} }
testeq("p532-all-33",   pass) { all{3|3} }   { array{3,3} }

# 2. Leftmost split under IterAll (hand-derived from Fig. 13 as transcribed):
#    all{(1|2)+(10|20)} = <11,21,12,22>; swapping the two choices' positions
#    gives a different tuple - the ordered-carrier witness pair.
testeq("p532-split-left",  pass) { all{(1|2)+(10|20)} } { array{11,21,12,22} }
testeq("p532-split-right", pass) { all{(10|20)+(1|2)} } { array{11,12,21,22} }

# 3. one{} takes the first candidate (Fig. 13 IterIf first-candidate reading).
testeq("p532-one-first",  pass) { one{2|1} }  { 2 }
testeq("p532-if-first",   pass) { if(x := 2|1){x}else{0} }  { 2 }

# 4. Commutativity witness with NO collector: one order gives a value, the
#    other is stuck.  Untestable under a commutative-idempotent reading.
testeq("p532-one-safe-first",   pass) { one{1|(1/0)} }   { 1 }
testeq("p532-one-stuck-first",  pass) { one{(1/0)|1} }   { wrong }

# 5. dotdot: the paper's printed rule (Fig. 10 line 459, glyph-verified
#    2026-11-27) enumerates as a CHOICE of integers, not a tuple value.
#    Flat enumeration pins (the kernel's tuple reading would make the second
#    pin produce array{array{1,2,3}}).
testeq("p532-dotdot-flat",   pass) { all{1..3} }   { array{1,2,3} }
testeq("p532-dotdot-one",    pass) { one{1..3} }   { 1 }
testeq("p532-dotdot-desc",   pass) { all{3..1} }   { array{} }
testeq("p532-dotdot-scan",   pass) { all{x := 1..3; x*2} }  { array{2,4,6} }

# 6. Division rows for the DEV-5 record (kernel claims: floored quotient,
#    zero divisor stuck-not-fail - these ask the oracle the same questions).
testeq("p532-div-floor-1",  pass) { 7/(0-2) }     { -4 }
testeq("p532-div-floor-2",  pass) { (0-7)/(0-2) } { 3 }
testeq("p532-div-floor-3",  pass) { (0-6)/(0-4) } { 1 }
testeq("p532-div-int",      pass) { 32/4 }        { 8 }
testeq("p532-div-zero",     pass) { 1/0 }         { wrong }
testeq("p532-div-zero-if",  pass) { if(x := 1/0){x}else{2} }  { wrong }
